{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Wooden door creak (low groan)",
  "description": "A massive oak cellar door on wooden pintle hinges, leaned open very slowly: no squeal at all, only wood groaning against wood. Each slip of the hinge is a small knock that the door leaf answers with its own woody resonances. The slips come one by one at first ('tok, tok, tok'), crowd together into a rattling purr and fuse into a low, straining groan as the door passes the middle, with a catch where it drops and recovers. Then it slows back through the purr to single knocks and stops, the timber settling with a low thud. A second, smaller joint (the top pintle) ticks along at its own slower pace.",
  "tags": [
    "door",
    "creak",
    "groan",
    "wood",
    "hinge",
    "cellar",
    "heavy",
    "slow",
    "ship",
    "timber",
    "horror",
    "low",
    "stick-slip"
  ],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 17,
  "tracks": [
